Test-only: usb-printer, a USB printer class device (USB Device Class
Definition for Printing Devices 1.1) for QEMU, with a qtest
(tests/qtest/usb-printer-test.c, 8 cases on qemu-xhci). Interface 07/01/02
(bulk OUT 0x01, bulk IN 0x82) or, with protocol=1, 07/01/01. It answers
GET_DEVICE_ID with the IEEE 1284 id of the device-id property,
GET_PORT_STATUS from the run-time properties paper-empty, error and offline
(qom-set), and SOFT_RESET (21h, and 23h as printer class 1.0 had it;
reset-other-only=on stalls 21h). Bulk OUT goes to the host file named by
file= (append=on to keep it); it is NAKed while busy is set or, with
hold-on-fault (default on), while a fault is raised; out-rate=<bytes/s>
paces it. Bulk IN returns a PJL status reply to "@PJL INFO STATUS" in the
OUT stream and bytes written to in-inject (ending a reply that fills its last
packet with a zero-length packet), and NAKs otherwise. A failed write of the
host file stalls bulk OUT from then on. Also
highspeed=on (a High Speed descriptor set beside the Full Speed one),
idvendor=/idproduct=, serial=, log=<file> (one line per request).
Applies to QEMU v11.1.0 after qemu-usbnet-hs.patch and
qemu-xhci-cancel.patch (tests/qtest/meson.build context). The emulator as a
whole remains GPL-2.0-or-later.
